```typescript
function countingSort(arr: number[]): number[] {
  // Finding the maximum and minimum values in the array
  let max = arr[0];
  let min = arr[0];
  for (let I = 1; I < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > max) {
      max = arr[i];
    }
    if (arr[i] < min) {
      min = arr[i];
    }
  }

  // Creating a count array of size range
  const range = max - min + 1;
  const count = new Array(range).fill(0);

  // Counting the frequency of each element in the array
  for (let I = 0; I < arr.length; i++) {
    count[arr[i] - min]++;
  }

  // Calculating the cumulative frequency
  for (let I = 1; I < range; i++) {
    count[i] += count[i - 1];
  }

  // Sorting the array
  const output = new Array(arr.length);
  for (let I = arr.length - 1; I >= 0; i--) {
    output[count[arr[i] - min] - 1] = arr[i];
    count[arr[i] - min]--;
  }

  // Returning the sorted array
  return output;
}
```

Counting sort is a sorting algorithm that works best when the range of the input values is small compared to the number of elements in the input array. It works by counting the frequency of each element in the input array, then calculating the cumulative frequency of each element. Finally, the output array is constructed by placing each element in its sorted position based on its cumulative frequency. 

In this implementation, we first find the maximum and minimum values in the input array to determine the range of values. We then create a count array of size range and count the frequency of each element in the input array. We then calculate the cumulative frequency of each element in the count array. Finally, we sort the input array by placing each element in its sorted position in the output array based on its cumulative frequency. The result is a sorted array with a time complexity of O(n+k), where n is the number of elements in the input array and k is the range of values in the input array.

