The function first performs error checking on the input parameters, throwing an error if any of them are invalid (i.e. Negative or zero values). If all inputs are valid, the function calculates the compounded interest using the formula `(1 + r/n)^nt`, where `r` is the interest rate, `n` is the number of times the interest is compounded per year (in this case, assumed to be yearly), and `t` is the duration of the loan in years. The function then multiplies the loan amount by the compounded interest to get the total amount owed, rounds it to 2 decimal places, and returns it.

